{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze the task carefully.\n\nThe task AGENT-TF-01 is about implementing a Toolformer-style API call filter. Let me understand the algorithm:\n\n1. For each call, compute: `gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call`\n2. Normalize gain by prediction tokens: `normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens`\n3. Accept a call if:\n   - `parseable == true`\n   - `normalized_gain \u003e= threshold`\n4. Return `accepted_call_ids` and `diagnostics` (in original order)\n\nThe output schema requires:\n- `accepted_call_ids`: list of strings\n- `diagnostics`: list of objects with `accepted` (bool), `call_id` (str), `normalized_gain` (number)\n\nLet me verify with the first fixture case:\n\nCase 0, threshold=0.05:\n- call0: gain = 1.94835097 - 0.38569502 = 1.56265595, norm_gain = 1.56265595/5 = 0.31253119, parseable=true → accepted\n- call1: gain = 1.06116273 - 0.68319969 = 0.37796304, norm_gain = 0.37796304/4 = 0.09449076, parseable=true → accepted\n- call2: gain = 1.21810502 - 0.47260371 = 0.74550131, norm_gain = 0.74550131/6 = 0.12425022, parseable=true → accepted\n- call3: gain = 1.05721833 - 0.29767903 = 0.7595393, norm_gain = 0.7595393/5 = 0.15190786, parseable=true → accepted\n- call4: gain = 1.06717367 - 0.85733566 = 0.20983801, norm_gain = 0.20983801/5 = 0.04196760, parseable=true → 0.04196760 \u003c 0.05 → NOT accepted\n- call5: gain = 1.66191711 - 0.89798497 = 0.76393214, norm_gain = 0.76393214/4 = 0.190983035, parseable=true → accepted\n\nSo accepted: call0, call1, call2, call3, call5\n\nFor case 2 (call4 has parseable=false):\n- call4: parseable=false → NOT accepted (regardless of gain)\n\nNow let me write the implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    \n    diagnostics = []\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    \n    for call in calls:\n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        prediction_tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        if prediction_tokens \u003c 1:\n            raise ValueError(f\"prediction_tokens must be \u003e= 1 for call {call_id}\")\n        \n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = round(gain / prediction_tokens, 10)  # keep as float\n        \n        accepted = parseable and normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"normalized_gain\": normalized_gain,\n            \"accepted\": accepted\n        })\n        \n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nWait, the candidate says \"Return accepted call IDs and rounded per-call diagnostics.\" - should I round the normalized_gain? The schema says type \"number\" so it can be a float. Let me not round to avoid precision issues, unless specified. Actually \"rounded\" is mentioned... maybe round to a certain number of decimal places? The schema just says \"number\" so I'll keep it as is.\n\nActually, I need to validate required fields. Let me add validation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    if \"threshold\" not in case:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing 'threshold' field\")\n    if \"calls\" not in case:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing 'calls' field\")\n    \n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    \n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"'calls' must be a list\")\n    \n    diagnostics = []\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    \n    for call in calls:\n        for field in (\"call_id\", \"loss_without_call\", \"loss_with_call\", \"prediction_tokens\", \"parseable\"):\n            if field not in call:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Missing field '{field}' in call\")\n        \n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        prediction_tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        if prediction_tokens \u003c 1:\n            raise ValueError(f\"prediction_tokens must be \u003e= 1 for call {call_id}\")\n        \n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens\n        \n        accepted = bool(parseable and normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"normalized_gain\": normalized_gain,\n            \"accepted\": accepted\n        })\n        \n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nNow I need to format this as a JSON string for the response envelope. The response must be:\n```json\n{\"implementation\": \"\u003cpython source as JSON string\u003e\"}\n```\n\nLet me prepare the final response.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    if \\\"threshold\\\" not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing 'threshold' field\\\")\\n    if \\\"calls\\\" not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing 'calls' field\\\")\\n\\n    threshold = case[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    calls = case[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n\\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"'calls' must be a list\\\")\\n\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n\\n    for call in calls:\\n        for field in (\\\"call_id\\\", \\\"loss_without_call\\\", \\\"loss_with_call\\\", \\\"prediction_tokens\\\", \\\"parseable\\\"):\\n            if field not in call:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"Missing field '{field}' in call\\\")\\n\\n        call_id = call[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        loss_without = call[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"]\\n        loss_with = call[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        prediction_tokens = call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"]\\n        parseable = call[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n\\n        if not isinstance(prediction_tokens, (int, float)) or prediction_tokens \u003c 1:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"prediction_tokens must be \u003e= 1 for call {call_id}\\\")\\n\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens\\n\\n        accepted = bool(parseable and normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\\n\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": normalized_gain,\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted\\n        })\\n\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01074lMCuBxZQxD5Gsj6QFnU","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2453},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2453,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":66,"output_tokens":1810,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1376},"service_tier":"standard"}}